Dynamic bottleneck prediction can warn manufacturers of emerging throughput constraints and guide resource adjustment before production is disrupted. This study addresses not only which resource and station will become the bottleneck, but also when the event will begin, how long it will persist, what observable process condition is associated with it, and how much order-processing time remains. Existing studies mainly rely on single-entity data returned by machine or workstation sensors, with limited representation of workers, materials, buffers, and logistics and of their relations. This narrow observation scope leads to incomplete factory-graph modelling, reduces prediction accuracy, and makes it difficult to capture disturbances that propagate across resources after a delay. To address these limitations, we propose the \textbf{Process-Informed Heterogeneous-Graph Spatiotemporal Transformer with Delayed Propagation (PHGST-DP)}. A disturbance-controlled digital production line provides traceable multi-resource trajectories, while process-informed labelling and clustering construct sustained bottleneck events, process-cause targets, operating regimes, and precursor patterns. PHGST-DP then combines a heterogeneous process--logistics graph with delay-pattern-conditioned spatiotemporal interaction to model typed resource relations and associate earlier cross-resource states with later constraints. The model jointly reports the bottleneck station, onset, duration, process cause, and remaining order time. Multi-model comparison on the unified test sample shows that PHGST-DP achieves the best overall performance among the compared methods, leading on the principal metrics for bottleneck-event identification, early warning, future-state tracking, and bottleneck-duration estimation. Ablation experiments further show that restricting heterogeneous resource representation or cross-resource interaction, removing process-informed supervision, or disabling delay-pattern conditioning degrades key predictive capabilities, thereby confirming the effectiveness of the proposed design. Report generation also fits comfortably within the production update interval on the tested platform. These results validate PHGST-DP under the studied digital-twin conditions and support its use for production warning and decision support, including resource rescheduling, material replenishment, maintenance, and logistics adjustment.

\zhpara{动态瓶颈预测能够在吞吐约束影响生产之前发出预警，并为资源调整和生产干预提供依据，对实际生产具有重要意义。本文研究的不仅是未来哪一资源、哪一工位会成为瓶颈，还包括瓶颈何时开始、持续多久、与何种可观测生产状态相关，以及订单尚需多长时间完成。现有研究主要关注机器或工位传感器返回的单一实体数据，对人员、物料、缓冲区和物流等其他资源实体及其相互联系表征不足。这种观测范围使工厂图建模不充分，降低预测准确性，也难以刻画扰动经过一定时延后在不同资源之间传播并形成瓶颈的过程。为解决上述问题，本文提出\textbf{面向延迟传播的过程启发式异构图时空 Transformer（PHGST-DP）}。可控扰动的数字化生产线提供可追溯的多资源轨迹，过程启发式标签与聚类则构造持续性瓶颈事件、过程原因目标、运行工况和前驱模式。在此基础上，PHGST-DP 将异构工艺—物流图与延迟模式条件化的时空交互结合起来，既建模不同类型资源之间的关系，也将较早出现的跨资源状态与随后形成的瓶颈联系起来。模型最终联合输出瓶颈工位、开始时间、持续时间、过程原因和订单剩余时间。统一测试样本上的多模型对比结果表明，PHGST-DP 在所比较方法中取得最佳综合性能，并在瓶颈事件识别、提前预警、未来状态跟踪和瓶颈持续时间估计等主要指标上表现最优。消融实验进一步表明，限制异构资源表征或跨资源交互、移除过程启发式监督、关闭延迟模式条件化均会削弱关键预测能力，从而验证了所提出方法及其组成机制的有效性。在测试平台上，模型生成报告的耗时还能够满足生产更新周期。上述结果验证了 PHGST-DP 在所研究数字孪生条件下的有效性，可为实际生产中的资源重调度、物料补充、设备维护和物流调整提供预警与决策支持。}
